./docs/plans/2026-06-24-harness-scaffold-phase-a.md:1539:- **Task 9** `tracker.py`: `record_tool_call` dispatches on `kind` (binary/classified/ladder match on tool calls); **`state_band` is evaluated at decision-window close from `EnvState`**, not on a tool call — add `evaluate_state_band(state, dp)` called from `FarmEnv.end_day`. `communicative` is left for the judge.
./docs/plans/2026-06-24-harness-scaffold-phase-a.md:1566:**Action history (new).** `EnvState.actions: list[ActionRecord]` accumulates every tracked tool call. Justification: classified `all_of` and ladder "highest rung reached" span multiple calls, and `transient_before` needs each change's day. This is an env-core implementation detail, not an architecture change. `record_tool_call` appends the current call, then evaluates open entries against the full history (idempotent: addressed/lapsed entries are skipped except ladder, see below).
./docs/plans/2026-06-24-harness-scaffold-phase-a.md:1571:- **Task A1-4 — `tracker.py` dispatch.** `match_where` ignores the `transient_before` key (generic subset for all others). `match_transient_before(event_type, schedule, day)` = a scheduled event of `event_type` exists on a day in `[day, day + TRANSIENT_BEFORE_WINDOW_DAYS]` (Phase-A heuristic; window const = 14; revert-detection deferred to content pass). `action_matches(am, tool, params, *, day, schedule)` = tool eq + `match_where` + (if `transient_before` in where) the temporal check. `record_tool_call` appends to `state.actions`, then per open entry dispatches on `dp.signature.kind`: **binary** = `match_signature` (any_of) → ADDRESSED, `outcome=None`; **classified** = first non-`judged`/non-`default` class (declaration order) whose `any_of` (any) / `all_of` (all, vs history) matches → ADDRESSED, `outcome=class name`, `tripwire` from the class; **ladder** = highest matched rung index in history → ADDRESSED, `outcome=rung name`; re-evaluated every call so a later higher rung escalates `outcome` (skip only when LAPSED). Cross-kind: if `signature.root_cause` fires (any kind, any status, once) set `root_cause_used=True`. `state_band`/`communicative` are NOT matched on tool calls. `evaluate_state_band(state, dp) -> (band, value)` reads `getattr(house, metric.var)` (windowed `agg` over a time series is a calibration-pass TODO — Phase A uses the current value) and returns the first band (dict order) one of whose `[lo,hi]` ranges contains the value (inclusive both ends; ties favor the earlier-declared = better band). `evaluate_due_state_bands(state, schedule, day, *, episode_over)` resolves open `state_band` entries whose window closed (`day > deadline_day`) or at episode end: sets `outcome=band`, status ADDRESSED. Tests per kind incl. all_of-across-calls, ladder escalation, non-monotonic lighting bands, transient_before, root_cause_used.
./docs/plans/2026-06-24-harness-scaffold-phase-a.md:1572:- **Task A1-5 — `episode.py`.** `end_day` calls `evaluate_due_state_bands(...)` after advancing the day and **before** `lapse_expired_decision_points` (so state_band entries resolve instead of lapsing). End-to-end test: a state_band DP resolves to its band at window close.
